## 3. Major Problems Encountered and Solutions

| Problem | Root cause | Solution | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Frontier explorer initially disabled | Manual activation required | Integrated automatic benchmark startup | ✅ |
| Oracle rejected frontier goals | Selected occupancy-grid goals were not necessarily NavMesh-feasible | Reused Qibin's Stage 4E batch feasibility filtering | ✅ |
| Robot failed to navigate | Earlier custom frontier-to-Oracle integration was incomplete | Switched to Qibin's existing Stage 4E pipeline | ✅ |
| Robot stopped after several goals | Original six-request predicate-binding budget | Added standalone-only budget bypass | ✅ |
| Oracle navigation timeouts | HM3D paths were longer than those in Qibin's MP3D experiments | Investigated and retained explicit timeout accounting | ⚠️ Some timeouts remain |
| Hydra TF extrapolation errors | Intermittent sensor/TF timing mismatch | Confirmed they were not responsible for the six-request termination | ⚠️ Intermittent |
| Missing evaluation outputs | Previous reporting tool did not provide a complete evaluation workflow | Integrated trajectory recording, evaluator, and reporting | ✅ |

### Important discovery

The repeated robot-stopping problem was **not caused by HM3D incompatibility, Hydra mapping failure, or TF errors**.

The actual cause was:

```text
first_binding_budget_exhausted
```

Qibin's original system limits the first predicate-binding stage to six navigation requests.

Because our standalone benchmark intentionally uses unbindable placeholder predicates, that condition could never be satisfied.

We implemented a benchmark-specific bypass while preserving the original predicate-task behavior.

