We completed an end-to-end LangMap episode:

**Episode:** `00800-TEEsavR23oF_instance_0`

### Navigation and mapping

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Official start position | `[-4.03902, 3.11338, -0.06032]` |
| Navigation requests | 11 |
| Successful Oracle requests | 8 |
| Failed/cancelled requests | 3 |
| Oracle timeouts | 2 |
| Executed actions | 500 |
| Actual traveled distance | 26.408 m |
| Hydra graph revision | 22 → 39 |
| Termination reason | `benchmark_action_limit_reached` |

### LangMap evaluation

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Shortest reference path | 8.387 m |
| Final target geodesic distance | 0.561 m |
| Minimum target distance during exploration | **0.098 m** |
| Success | False |
| SR (one episode) | 0% |
| SPL | 0.0 |

### Interpretation

The robot successfully explored the environment and passed within:

\[
d_{\min}=0.098\text{ m}
\]

of a valid target viewpoint.

However, its final position was:

\[
d_{\text{final}}=0.561\text{ m}
\]

Therefore, it failed the official terminal-position success criterion.

**This is an important validation result: the evaluator distinguishes passing through the target region from successfully terminating inside it.**

The result also demonstrates why future target-aware reasoning and stopping decisions matter.

